					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1889641#post-2661836</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1889641/history#post-2661836</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 27 Sep 2016 22:10:10 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Humanmale</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2785893</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The message was deliberately mixed.</p> <p>These people aren't any one thing. Not all beaten down, not all ill-educated, not all long-term prisoners. They're just people. I was trying to show them living their lives as best they can under the circumstances.</p> <p>It's the Foundation that tries to make them one thing, perhaps to make them nothing in an effort to justify what it does to them.</p> <p>Obviously I didn't get that across as well as I could have.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1889641#post-2661809</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1889641/history#post-2661809</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 27 Sep 2016 20:40:39 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Kalinin</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2203795</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Neutral vote, because I find the structure of this to be clever. Pretty cool way to tell a story.</p> <p>My issue is that the messages about who these people were is pretty mixed. On the one hand, these seem like people who are pretty familiar with how prison life works (or at least popular conception of how prison life works). However, stuff like the &quot;I can't believe it's not brandy&quot; line are like something a smart-alecky, fairly educated twenty-something would say, who are typically not the kind of folks who go to prison. It also bespeaks a lightheartedness that I think would be fairly hard to come by in the environment you're portraying. It's kind of like a homeless guy with a funny sign. Most likely hasn't been homeless long.</p> <p>The delivery system is solid, but the payload is a little too muddled in what it's conveying to me for me to upvote.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
